/ActualText (Three panels of line graphs show SE&#x00025; and log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029; trends against total sample size across three cases.</alt-text><long-desc>The figure presents three line graphs labeled CASE I, CASE II, and CASE III. The x-axis represents total sample size &#x00028;in increments of 10^4&#x00029;, while the y-axis displays SE&#x00025; and log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029;. - &#x0002A;&#x0002A;Panel I:&#x0002A;&#x0002A; Multiple methods show decreasing SE&#x00025; and log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029; trends, with "Input" highest in SE&#x00025; and "GLO" consistently lowest in log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029;. - &#x0002A;&#x0002A;Panel II:&#x0002A;&#x0002A; Similar trends appear, with "Input" retaining the highest SE&#x00025; values; log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029; dips with increasing sample sizes, GLO remains the best performer. - &#x0002A;&#x0002A;Panel III:&#x0002A;&#x0002A; Displays pronounced downward trends in both metrics. "Input" still peaks in SE&#x00025;, while "GLO" hits its lowest log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029; around -7&#x00025;. Overall, all cases indicate decreasing trends in error percentages with increased sample sizes.)
/A 223 0 R
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/S /Figure
/T ()
/Pg 18 0 R
/Alt (Three panels of line graphs show SE&#x00025; and log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029; trends against total sample size across three cases.</alt-text><long-desc>The figure presents three line graphs labeled CASE I, CASE II, and CASE III. The x-axis represents total sample size &#x00028;in increments of 10^4&#x00029;, while the y-axis displays SE&#x00025; and log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029;. - &#x0002A;&#x0002A;Panel I:&#x0002A;&#x0002A; Multiple methods show decreasing SE&#x00025; and log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029; trends, with "Input" highest in SE&#x00025; and "GLO" consistently lowest in log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029;. - &#x0002A;&#x0002A;Panel II:&#x0002A;&#x0002A; Similar trends appear, with "Input" retaining the highest SE&#x00025; values; log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029; dips with increasing sample sizes, GLO remains the best performer. - &#x0002A;&#x0002A;Panel III:&#x0002A;&#x0002A; Displays pronounced downward trends in both metrics. "Input" still peaks in SE&#x00025;, while "GLO" hits its lowest log&#x00028;MSE&#x00029; around -7&#x00025;. Overall, all cases indicate decreasing trends in error percentages with increased sample sizes.)
